{
  "name": "Score French customer credit risk weekly with Sirenic and Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Score French customer credit risk weekly\n\n**Disclaimer: this template uses the Sirenic community node, so it runs on self-hosted n8n only.**\n\n### Who's it for\nCredit managers and finance teams carrying receivables on French customers.\n\n### How it works\nEvery Monday the workflow reads your customer sheet, calls Sirenic's default risk score for each SIREN ($0.10) and writes back the score (0-100), its class, the 12-month risk wording and the reference financial year. The score is deterministic — it comes with its component axes (liquidity, profitability, structure) and its model version, so any decision you take on it stays explainable. A Slack digest reports only the customers whose class CHANGED since the previous run, so nobody gets spammed with a stable portfolio. Failed requests are never billed.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Install the n8n-nodes-sirenic community node and create Sirenic credentials.\n2. Prepare a Google Sheet with columns: `SIREN`, `Company`, `Class` (left empty on first run), `Score`, `Checked at`.\n3. Select that sheet in both Google Sheets nodes and pick your Slack channel.\n4. Run once manually to fill the baseline, then let the schedule take over.\n\n### Requirements\nSelf-hosted n8n · Sirenic community node (pay-per-call, no subscription) · Google Sheets and Slack credentials. Budget: $0.10 per customer per run — keep the sheet to customers with real exposure.\n\n### How to customize\nDrive credit limits directly from the class; switch the schedule to monthly for a large book; push the score into your ERP instead of Sheets.",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 500
      },
      "id": "sticky-main-t07",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -820,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Read the customer book\nOne row per customer with an exposure. The loop processes them one at a time so a single failure never aborts the run.",
        "height": 150,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky-step1-t07",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        30
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Alert on CHANGE, not on state\nThe IF compares the fresh class with the one stored in the sheet. A stable portfolio produces no Slack noise — only downgrades and upgrades surface.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky-step2-t07",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        520,
        760
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "weeks",
              "triggerAtDay": [
                1
              ],
              "triggerAtHour": 7
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "schedule-t07",
      "name": "Every Monday morning",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -200,
        240
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "sheets-read-t07",
      "name": "Read customer book",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        20,
        240
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "reset": false
        }
      },
      "id": "loop-t07",
      "name": "One customer at a time",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitInBatches",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [
        240,
        240
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "dueDiligence",
        "operation": "getFailureScore",
        "siren": "={{ $json.SIREN }}"
      },
      "id": "sirenic-score-t07",
      "name": "Get default risk score",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-sirenic.sirenic",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        480,
        340
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "cond-changed",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.classe }}",
              "rightValue": "={{ $('One customer at a time').item.json.Class }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEquals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "if-changed-t07",
      "name": "Class changed?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        700,
        340
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "select": "channel",
        "channelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "text": "=:chart_with_upwards_trend: *Credit risk class changed*\n{{ $json.denomination }} (SIREN {{ $json.siren }})\n*{{ $('One customer at a time').item.json.Class || 'no baseline' }}* → *{{ $json.classe }}* · score {{ $json.score_risque }}/100 · 12-month risk: {{ $json.risque_12m }}\nDrivers: {{ ($json.composantes || []).map(c => c.axe + ' ' + c.indicateur + '=' + c.valeur).join(' · ') }}\nReference year {{ $json.exercice_reference }} · confidence {{ $json.confiance }} · model {{ $json.version_modele }}\n_Decision-support indicator, not a solvency opinion._",
        "otherOptions": {}
      },
      "id": "slack-changed-t07",
      "name": "Report the change on Slack",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        940,
        240
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "appendOrUpdate",
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "value": {
            "SIREN": "={{ $json.siren }}",
            "Company": "={{ $json.denomination }}",
            "Class": "={{ $json.classe }}",
            "Score": "={{ $json.score_risque }}",
            "Checked at": "={{ $now.toISO() }}"
          },
          "matchingColumns": [
            "SIREN"
          ],
          "schema": []
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "sheets-write-t07",
      "name": "Store the new score",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        940,
        440
      ]
    }
  ],
